      "t": "h",
      "text": "Handheld rule"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Keep the shutter at least **1/focal length**: 200 mm needs 1/200 s. On APS-C cameras such as the Canon R10, multiply the focal length by 1.6 first. Image stabilisation lets you go a few stops slower."
    },
    {
      "t": "note",
      "tone": "no",
      "text": "For video, shutter speed follows the frame rate. See the lesson on the 180° shutter rule."
    },
